Workshop


HANDS-ON WITH THE NEW CLI

2026-09-24 · 14:00–15:30 UTC

Where

Room 4B, HQ — or join on Zoom

Join

https://example.com/zoom/cli-workshop

A 90-minute working session for anyone shipping with the toolchain. Bring a laptop with Node 24 installed — we'll build a small integration together and leave with something that runs.


WHO IT'S FOR

 * Engineers wiring the CLI into a pipeline for the first time
 * Anyone who tried it, got stuck, and wants a second pass with help in the room


BEFORE YOU ARRIVE

 1. Install Node 24 (node --version should print v24.x or newer).
 2. Clone the starter repo from the registration page.
 3. Run npm install once so the first exercise isn't a waiting game.

> Seats are capped at 20 so everyone gets hands-on time. Can't make it? The recording and notes go out to all attendees.


MEET THE HOSTS

Alex Rivera

Developer Experience Lead

Builds the CLI workflows and integration patterns used across our engineering teams.

Sam Chen

Senior Platform Engineer

Maintains the internal toolchain and helps teams debug complex build and deployment issues.


AGENDA

14:00

Setup & orientation

14:20

Build your first integration, step by step

15:00

Debugging, gotchas, and open Q&A

----------------------------------------

NAAD

Flowing intelligence across the network.

